a shiny new Dragon Gets serenaded In the  final episode of season one of House of  the Dragon but which Dragon was that and  where did it come from spoilers ahead  the finale of House of the Dragon season  1 is finally here bringing with it the  true beginning of the Targaryen civil  war known as the dance of the Dragons  prior to the episode's jaw-dropping  climax Damon Targaryen and the rest of  the blacks loyal to Queen rhaenyra  Targaryen devised a strategy for their  inevitable conflict with the greens a  faction led by Queen Alison Hightower  and King aegon II during these battle  preparations much is made of the fact  that the blacks have a far greater  number of dragons than the greens  special typically they currently own  seven dragons to the greens four though  one of those four is Veigar the largest  dragon in the land on top of that Damon  also asserts that there are a slew of  unclaimed dragons which can still be  claimed and bound to their cause  including the legendary Verma Thor and  Silverwing who both reside on the dragon  mount that puts the final Dragon count  at Dragonstone has 13 to their fall  I also have a score of eggs incubating  in the dragon Mound  later in the episode we actually see  Damon singing in High Valyrian to Verma  Thor in a cave though you may not have  realized it at the time since this  immense bronze dragon is only identified  through subtitles adding to the  confusion is the fact that we aren't  given information about how Verma Thor  first arrived on dragon mount nor who  his writer was before he landed there  but the show's Source material Fire and  Blood has the answers minor spoilers for  that book starting now to understand the  importance of Verma Thor nicknamed the  bronze Fury for his unmistakable bronze  hide you first have to recognize the  fact that his first writer was none  other than King jaharis Targaryen the  first who we first met back in episode 1  during a flashback to the great Council  of 101 AC wherein he named viserys as  his Heir vermouthor stayed by King  joharis's side until the King's death at  which point the dragon fled to a cavern  within the volcano known as the dragon  mount Verma Thor has since brooded there  throughout the entire reign of King  viserys and when we meet him in House of  the Dragon he's nearly 100 years old in  the books it said that only vegar and  balerion the black dread aegon the  conqueror's dragon were larger than  vermouthor making him the second largest  dragon in all of House of the dragon and  an important weapon for the blacks  should they successfully claim him for  their side despite the fact that we  don't see any other dragons during  Damon's surprising confrontation with  firmathor it's worth noting that he  shares his home on the dragon Mound with  another riderless Dragon Silverwing  originally the dragon of Queen alisan  Targaryen wife of King jaharis according  to the Fire and Blood chapter the dying  of the Dragons It's said that Silverwing  and vermouthor also made it following  their writer's deaths and although their  specific lineage is not confirmed within  the books this is significant due to  Damon's previous claim about having a  score of eggs incubating in the dragon  mount indeed on top of the potential  power that would be brought to the  blacks should they successfully claim  the mass of vermouthor it's possible  that vermouthor and Silverwing have  provided them with another clutch of  eggs to secure the future of their  faction although it's currently unclear  what role Verma Thor will play in the  next season of House of the Dragon his  expected appearance in the season finale  makes it clear that he and his potential  brood of eggs could become an important  part of the story moving forward
 

